==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gmw-pro|gem-pro|ine-pro|inh=2}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|vinden}}, from {{inh|de|goh|findan}}. Cognate with {{cog|nds|finden}}, {{cog|nl|vinden}}, {{cog|en|find}}, {{cog|da|finde}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|[ˈfɪndn̩]|[ˈfɪndən]}}
* {{rhymes|de|ɪndn̩|s=2}}
* {{audio|de|De-finden.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-finden.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|finden<fand,gefunden,fände>}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[find]]; to [[discover]]
#: {{ux|de|Ich habe deine Schlüssel '''gefunden'''.|I '''found''' your keys.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|with a predicate adjective or predicate noun (accusative)}}  to [[think]] that (something) is (a certain way); to [[consider]] (something) to be (a certain way); to [[find]]
#: {{ux|de|'''Findest''' du mich interessant?|Do you '''find''' me interesting?}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to find one’s way

====Conjugation====
